{"name":"King’s Ransom","hex":"#b59d77","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"king’s ransom","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very large sum of money."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/king%E2%80%99s_ransom"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ransom","blocks":[{"text":"Ransom is the practice of holding a prisoner or item to extort money or property to secure their release. It also refers to the sum of money paid by the other party to secure a captive's freedom. It can also refer to paying such a ransom."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/The_Ransom_by_John_Everett_Millais%2C_1860-62.JPG/330px-The_Ransom_by_John_Everett_Millais%2C_1860-62.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ransom","wikidata":"Q1414572"},{"title":"King","blocks":[{"text":"King is a royal title given to a male monarch. A king is an absolute monarch if he holds unrestricted governmental power or exercises full sovereignty over a nation. In a modern context, the title may refer to the ruler of one of a number of modern monarchies. The title of king is used alongside other titles for monarchs: in the West, emperor, grand prince, prince, archduke, duke or grand duke, and in the Islamic world, malik, sultan, emir or hakim, among others."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Aachen_Domschatz_Bueste1.jpg/330px-Aachen_Domschatz_Bueste1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King","wikidata":"Q12097"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/March_2017-_Coors_Kidnapping_Ransom_Note_%2833460504411%29.jpg/500px-March_2017-_Coors_Kidnapping_Ransom_Note_%2833460504411%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/March_2017-_Coors_Kidna